# Peregrine Creative Group — Design System

Reference: [AIRCO](https://www.aircompany.com/company) — full-bleed immersive hero, commanding typography, ultra-clean layout, cinematic imagery, and editorial precision.

---

## Design Philosophy

The site should feel like a modern industrial brand with depth and confidence. Not a startup, not a portfolio — a capable operating company presented with the visual clarity and restraint of a premium brand.

Key principles from AIRCO reference:
- **Immersive heroes** — full-bleed imagery with large overlaid type, no box constraints
- **Typography as architecture** — headlines are the primary visual element, not imagery
- **Generous whitespace** — sections breathe with extreme vertical spacing
- **Minimal chrome** — no borders, no cards where unnecessary, content does the work
- **Dark/light contrast** — alternating dark feature sections with clean white editorial
- **Cinematic imagery** — editorial, high-quality, atmospheric (not stock)

---

## Layout Philosophy

### Grid & Container
- Max container width: `max-w-7xl` (1280px)
- Horizontal padding: `px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-16`
- Use 12-column grids for split layouts: `md:grid-cols-12`
- Common splits: 5/7, 6/6, 7/5 columns
- Full-bleed sections break out of container for impact

### Section Rhythm
- Extreme vertical whitespace: `py-32 md:py-40 lg:py-48`
- Hero: full viewport `min-h-screen` with content anchored
- Dark feature sections: `py-32 md:py-44`
- No visible separators between sections — use whitespace and background colour changes instead
- Let content breathe — less is more

### Spacing Principles
- Headings get large vertical space before body copy: `mb-8` to `mb-12`
- Paragraphs after headings: `mt-6` to `mt-8`
- Section internal gaps: `gap-12` to `gap-20`
- Avoid tight groupings — editorial spread is the goal

---

## Typography

### Font
- Primary: Inter (weights 300, 400, 500, 600)
- System fallback: `-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif`

### Scale (AIRCO-inspired — large and commanding)
- Hero headline: `text-5xl md:text-6xl lg:text-7xl font-light leading-[1.05]` — enormous, light, cinematic
- Section headings (h2): `text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-light leading-[1.1]`
- Statement text (large body): `text-xl md:text-2xl font-light leading-relaxed` — used for key paragraphs
- Subheadings (h3): `text-xl md:text-2xl font-medium`
- Body: `text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed`
- Small/supporting: `text-sm leading-relaxed`
- Eyebrow labels: `text-xs font-medium tracking-[0.15em] uppercase`

### Weight Usage
- `font-light` (300): hero headlines, large section titles, statement paragraphs — the dominant weight
- `font-normal` (400): body copy
- `font-medium` (500): subheadings, card titles, nav links, emphasis
- `font-semibold` (600): button labels, key names, active states only

### Tracking
- Large headlines: `tracking-tight` or `tracking-[-0.02em]`
- Body text: default
- Eyebrow/label: `tracking-[0.15em]`
- Button text: `tracking-wide`

---

## Colour Palette

### Light Sections
- Page background: `bg-white`
- Primary text: `text-neutral-900`
- Body text: `text-neutral-600`
- Muted/secondary: `text-neutral-500`
- Eyebrow/labels: `text-neutral-400`
- Borders (when needed): `border-neutral-100` — very subtle

### Dark Sections (immersive brand moments)
- Background: `bg-neutral-950` or `bg-[#0a0a0a]` — near true black
- Alternative dark: `bg-[#1a2f3f]` — deep blue-teal (for footer)
- Primary text: `text-white`
- Body text: `text-white/70`
- Secondary: `text-white/50`
- Muted: `text-white/30`

### Accent Usage
- Accents used very sparingly — primarily in interactive states or tiny indicators
- Green for sustainability: `text-green-500`
- No bright accent colours in headings or large text — keep it monochromatic

